A diverse group of children gathered around a glowing computer terminal embedded in a weathered brick wall in an Indian village courtyard, their faces illuminated by the screen's warm light as they lean in with intense curiosity and excitement, discovering knowledge together without any adult supervision. The scene is rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive post-impressionist style with swirling brushstrokes in the deep blue evening sky above, thick impasto technique creating texture in the crumbling ochre and terracotta walls, and vibrant yellows and oranges radiating from the screen like a small sun. Scattered around the courtyard are traditional elements—clay pots, a sleeping dog, laundry on a line—all rendered with expressive, energetic brushwork. The children's clothing features bold, saturated colors typical of van Gogh's palette. A single banyan tree with twisting branches frames the scene, its leaves painted in swirling patterns against the starry twilight sky, suggesting the organic, self-organizing nature of learning itself.
